ONNX Runtime 1.30.0 WebGPU Split: run a node with more outputs than the
device's maxStorageBuffersPerShaderStage allows (beside the input) as several
programs, each writing one batch of the outputs, as Concat already does with
its inputs. Adreno 830 allows 16, and BiRefNet's decoder splits into up to 33
outputs, so its Split nodes failed with "Too many storage buffers in shader".
A node within the limit runs the one program it ran before.

--- a/onnxruntime/core/providers/webgpu/tensor/split.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/providers/webgpu/tensor/split.cc
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
